WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:02.900
- Have you ever gotten a
notice that looks like this?

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:04.560
It looks like a scam, right?

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.780
It looks like it can't possibly be true.

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:09.410
But this is a notice of a
class action settlement.

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:11.330
And there's actually a very good chance

00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:12.720
that this is on the level.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:14.530
And it's possible that you stand

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:15.960
to make some money off of it,

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:18.360
or at least get something of value.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:19.890
But you'd be forgiven if you thought

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:21.904
that this was complete
nonsense, because I mean,

00:00:21.904 --> 00:00:23.454
just look at it.

00:00:23.454 --> 00:00:26.130
Look, lawyers are good
at writing things down.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:28.010
They are not great at graphic design.

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:29.630
But the biggest question
is, what do you do

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:30.910
when you get a notice like this?

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:32.460
How do you know if it's real?

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:34.670
Well, as it happens,
your favorite bird lawyer

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:36.470
has actually litigated and settled

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:38.850
countless numbers of
class action settlements

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:40.970
worth hundreds of millions of dollars.

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:42.590
So let's talk about the good, the bad,

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:45.310
and the extremely ugly
about class action lawsuits.

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:47.170
And most importantly, what you should do

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:49.330
if you get a notice of
class action settlement.

00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:52.303
So join me as I spill some legal tea.

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:00.050
Sponsored by Trade Coffee.

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:02.550
So this is no joke, I really
did receive this notice

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:05.870
of class action settlement
related to an Epic Games lawsuit.

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:08.280
Apparently, at some point
I played either Fortnite

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:12.210
or Rocket League, and I might
be entitled to some money

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:14.210
or some benefits as a
result of this settlement.

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:16.230
It makes sense, because I
will never get that time

00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:17.970
that I spent on Fortnight back.

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:20.660
So I would really, really like
to be compensated for that.

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:21.910
And the things that we're
gonna talk about today

00:01:21.910 --> 00:01:24.850
will relate to this particular
class action lawsuit,

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:27.740
but it should apply to just
about any class action notice

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:28.900
that you receive.

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:31.730
So let's first talk about
what is a class action suit,

00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:33.930
because this is one of the
most misunderstood things

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:34.960
in all of law.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:36.490
Generally, when you have a lawsuit,

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:39.490
you personally sue somebody
else, because the dollar amounts

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:41.580
in question are worth
getting compensation for

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:43.400
what you think you were wronged over.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.900
But a class action is
the opposite of that.

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:48.320
It's where a lot of people
were probably harmed

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:51.270
in very, very small ways that
it would never make sense

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:53.320
for them to individually file suit.

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:55.830
But instead, if you wrap
all of them together,

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:57.770
the class of people, all of those people

00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:00.510
who are in the same situation,
can get compensation

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:03.460
from the company or another individual.

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:04.880
And when you group them all together,

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:06.740
it makes it worthwhile to file suit.

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:08.430
Part of it is a punitive reason.

00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:11.340
We don't want companies
to engage in misbehavior

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:13.900
that they'd never
otherwise be punished for

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:16.650
because simply the
individuals would never think

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:18.420
to hire their own personal attorney.

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:21.680
So every state and the
federal system has laws

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:23.940
on the books to allow people
to file a class action.

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:25.650
And a class action gets this reputation

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:26.600
that's sort of like Rico.

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:28.180
If you file a class action,

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:30.530
then it's a super, super serious lawsuit.

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:33.750
And a class action can deal
with large dollar amounts,

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:35.060
especially because you're aggregating

00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:36.510
a whole bunch of claims.

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:39.040
But just because it's a
class action doesn't mean

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:43.210
that it's necessarily a super
scary or super nasty lawsuit.

00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:44.810
Sometimes class actions settle

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:46.330
for hundreds of millions of dollars,

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:47.390
sometimes they go to trial,

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:49.260
and sometimes they're simply dismissed

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:50.930
and no one gets anything.

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:52.160
But the most important thing to remember

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:54.930
about a class action is
that it requires a class,

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:57.490
a group of people who
suffered a similar injury,

00:02:57.490 --> 00:02:59.670
that all of their injuries
and all of the things

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:02.160
that happened to them
are very, very similar.

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:04.940
Because a court is not going
to engage in a class action

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:08.360
if it has to individually
look at every single person.

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:10.760
If the calculation that
goes into the damages

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:12.540
for each individual person is different,

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:15.510
it's probably not likely to
give rise to a class action.

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:17.660
The class has to be very similar.

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:19.970
The damages that they suffered
have to be very similar.

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:22.860
And it has to be easy for
the court to ascertain all

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:25.480
of these things together
there, because they're dealing

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:27.270
with potentially hundreds, thousands,

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:29.624
and sometimes even millions of people.

00:03:29.624 --> 00:03:31.050
So imagine, if you will, a person runs

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:33.510
into a crowd and just
starts punching people.

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:35.860
Now, it could be that
that person has punched

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:37.403
a hundred people in that
crowd, and you might think

00:03:37.403 --> 00:03:40.270
that could give rise to a
class action, but probably not,

00:03:40.270 --> 00:03:42.880
because maybe one person
was punched in the stomach,

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:44.808
one person was punched in the face,

00:03:44.808 --> 00:03:48.180
one person suffered a broken bone,

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:50.670
and one person was barely damaged at all.

00:03:50.670 --> 00:03:54.240
Because all of those injuries
are so fact specific,

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:56.090
that's not the kind of
thing that gives rise

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:57.256
to a class action.

00:03:57.256 --> 00:03:58.270
But on the other hand,
let's look at something

00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:00.700
that could be easily
adjudicated as a class action.

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:03.100
Let's imagine that there's
a big cell phone provider,

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:07.180
and let's say that they
improperly put a $1 fee

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:09.140
on your bill that shouldn't be there.

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:12.150
And let's say they bill that
out to a million customers.

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:13.950
Well, it's really easy to
ascertain those people.

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:15.460
You just look at the spreadsheet of

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:17.700
what people were charged what fees,

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:18.850
and the damages are all the same.

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:21.200
It's just that one extra
fee that shouldn't be there.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:22.810
That's exactly the kinds of fact situation

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:25.020
that's likely to give rise to a valuable

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:26.990
and valid class action lawsuit.

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:28.900
So now let's turn to this Fortnite

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:31.730
and Rocket League lawsuit
and use that as an example of

00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:34.300
what happens when a
class action has filed.

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:36.300
And here, because this court
case has already gotten

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:38.620
to the settlement stage,
all the documents are

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:41.530
helpfully displayed right on
the court settlement website.

00:04:41.530 --> 00:04:43.350
And yes, this website is legitimate.

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:44.640
It's not meant to look good,

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:46.760
it's just meant to be legally sufficient.

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:49.330
So what the plaintiffs
originally alleged is

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:52.560
that the makers of Fortnite
and Rocket League engaged

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:54.610
in some unfair business practices.

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:57.220
And in particular, if you
dig into the complaint,

00:04:57.220 --> 00:04:58.730
what you'll see is that
the plaintiff alleged

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:01.600
that a lot of minors
entered into transactions

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:04.410
on these video games and
weren't allowed to back out

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:07.310
of these transactions
because they were minors.

00:05:07.310 --> 00:05:09.871
And it also alleges some other
unfair business practices,

00:05:09.871 --> 00:05:12.740
as well as some claims
related to random loot crates

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:15.100
and people spending a
thousand virtual dollars

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:17.120
on loot crate related things.

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:19.300
We'll never know if that
was in fact true or not,

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:20.950
because one of the
benefits of settlement is

00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:23.560
that you don't have to go
through the expense of discovery

00:05:23.560 --> 00:05:25.450
and the whole trial to get to the truth

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:27.670
of the matter asserted,
you can just settle

00:05:27.670 --> 00:05:29.350
and say that you're not admitting anything

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:31.520
or you're not admitting fault,
if you're the defendant.

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:33.280
And here the parties
engaged in litigation,

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:35.360
but eventually came to
the conclusion that it was

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:37.630
in everyone's best interest
to settle the claims

00:05:37.630 --> 00:05:40.180
instead of spending
money on the litigation.

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:42.211
Now, when you come to that conclusion,

00:05:42.211 --> 00:05:45.310
it's not as easy as just
signing on the dotted line.

00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:48.280
In fact, both the plaintiffs
and the defendants

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:50.170
have to go to the court to get the court

00:05:50.170 --> 00:05:52.200
to sign off on the settlement itself.

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:53.710
It has to be court approved.

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:55.960
The court has to make sure
that the class of people

00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:57.790
are actually being fairly compensated

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:59.920
and that everything else is on the level.

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:01.720
Now, in addition to that,
you have to determine

00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:03.750
certain things, like what is the class.

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:06.047
And here, based on the
notice, it says that

00:06:06.047 --> 00:06:07.360
"You're a member of the settlement class

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:09.862
if at any time between July 1, 2015

00:06:09.862 --> 00:06:12.420
and February 25, 2021, you got a Fortnite

00:06:12.420 --> 00:06:15.330
or Rocket League account that
you used to play either game

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:18.300
on any device in any mod
and A, exchanged in-game

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:20.720
virtual currency for any in-game benefit

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:22.760
or B, made a purchase of virtual currency

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:24.450
or other in-game benefit for use

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:26.000
within Fortnite or Rocket League."

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:27.570
So if you fit that description,

00:06:27.570 --> 00:06:30.330
you're entitled to some
relief from the court.

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:31.780
And if you look at the
settlement agreement,

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:33.780
the lawyers estimate that
there were approximately

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:35.598
12 million people who have accounts

00:06:35.598 --> 00:06:38.466
who played the games
and fit that description

00:06:38.466 --> 00:06:41.080
across both Fortnite and Rocket League.

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:43.770
And now we get to the part
that everyone is waiting for.

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:46.260
What could you possibly
get out of this settlement?

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:48.350
Well, here, the defendants
have agreed to spend

00:06:48.350 --> 00:06:52.408
up to $26.5 million, but
that's unfortunately not

00:06:52.408 --> 00:06:54.780
what the class is going to get.

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:57.020
And here's where things
get a little bit ugly,

00:06:57.020 --> 00:06:58.500
and where I'm afraid we're going to have

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:00.703
to spill a little bit of legal tea.

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:04.250
Because the thing is,
the plaintiffs' lawyers

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:07.820
are not only negotiating on
behalf of the class of people

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:09.830
who were injured, but
they're also negotiating

00:07:09.830 --> 00:07:10.990
on behalf of themselves,

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:13.610
because they're going to
get a cut of this payout.

00:07:13.610 --> 00:07:16.930
Sometimes that payout might
be 10% of the class payout.

00:07:16.930 --> 00:07:19.830
Sometimes it might be 50
or 60% of the class payout.

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:21.900
But the good news is that
the court is supervising

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:23.570
all of this, and they're
trying to make sure

00:07:23.570 --> 00:07:25.810
that the lawyers aren't
taking too, too much

00:07:25.810 --> 00:07:26.850
from the class settlement.

00:07:26.850 --> 00:07:28.420
Look, the lawyers have to get paid.

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:31.190
If it weren't for them, these
suits would never be filed.

00:07:31.190 --> 00:07:33.670
But there's a fine line between
being compensated fairly

00:07:33.670 --> 00:07:36.820
for your time and also just
getting a huge windfall.

00:07:36.820 --> 00:07:38.750
But in addition to the
plaintiffs' lawyers,

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:40.650
there's also the class representative.

00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:42.490
To be able to file a class action,

00:07:42.490 --> 00:07:44.710
you have to have an
individual who represents

00:07:44.710 --> 00:07:46.520
the rest of the class fairly.

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:50.730
And that person or individuals
also need to be compensated.

00:07:50.730 --> 00:07:53.100
Generally, they're not paid all that much,

00:07:53.100 --> 00:07:55.810
maybe five to $10,000 at most.

00:07:55.810 --> 00:07:57.100
And sure, that's a lot of money,

00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:58.970
but your average class
representative is gonna

00:07:58.970 --> 00:07:59.900
put in a lot of work.

00:07:59.900 --> 00:08:01.270
They're probably gonna need to be deposed.

00:08:01.270 --> 00:08:02.840
They'll have to talk to the lawyers.

00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:04.720
And I wouldn't wish that on anyone.

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:06.810
So in the grand scheme
of things, the payout

00:08:06.810 --> 00:08:09.089
for the class representative
is usually not a huge amount

00:08:09.089 --> 00:08:11.530
as represented by the total payout.

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:13.923
So how much will the class actually get?

00:08:15.710 --> 00:08:17.680
Well, that depends on how many people

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:19.540
actually take up the settlement,

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:21.010
because it's a bit of a moving target.

00:08:21.010 --> 00:08:22.999
The more people that sign
up for the class action,

00:08:22.999 --> 00:08:25.420
the less each individual gets.

00:08:25.420 --> 00:08:27.350
And believe me, the fact
that I'm making a video

00:08:27.350 --> 00:08:29.620
about this is going to give the lawyers

00:08:29.620 --> 00:08:31.960
who are in charge of the
settlement, both on the defense

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:34.410
and the plaintiff side,
a complete heart attack,

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:37.420
because now I've publicized this suit,

00:08:37.420 --> 00:08:40.900
and the uptick on the number
of people who are going to ask

00:08:40.900 --> 00:08:43.800
for a class payment is probably
gonna go through the roof.

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:45.350
So, sorry, guys.

00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:47.630
So what will any
individual class member get

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:50.600
as a result if they participate
in this class action?

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:52.180
Well, you have to look at
the settlement agreement,

00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:55.430
but they might be able
to get a maximum of $50.

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:57.880
Depends on what kind of
damages you suffered.

00:08:57.880 --> 00:09:00.450
Or you have the option to receive payments

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:02.520
in virtual dollars, V-Bucks on Fortnite

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:06.180
or Rocket League, up
to a maximum of 13,500,

00:09:06.180 --> 00:09:09.162
which they estimate to be
worth about a hundred dollars

00:09:09.162 --> 00:09:11.270
if you had to purchase them in-game.

00:09:11.270 --> 00:09:12.910
Now, of course, the
virtual dollars are not

00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:15.270
actually worth a hundred dollars
to the game manufacturers,

00:09:15.270 --> 00:09:17.320
despite the fact that that's
how much it might cost you

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:18.820
if you wanted to buy them.

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:21.850
So they would much rather you
take your settlement payment

00:09:21.850 --> 00:09:23.160
in the form of the virtual dollars

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:24.640
instead of an actual cash payment.

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:26.690
So people who are members
of this punitive class

00:09:26.690 --> 00:09:27.710
have a couple of options.

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:30.160
They can go to this
website, they can sign up,

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:31.760
and they can say that they actively want

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:34.130
the additional benefit of either the cash

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:36.760
or the virtual dollars
as part of a payment

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:38.560
for this class action lawsuit.

00:09:38.560 --> 00:09:40.760
People, of course, can do nothing as well.

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:42.440
That's what most people do.

00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:44.210
They look at these
emails and these notices

00:09:44.210 --> 00:09:45.749
and they think that
this is a complete scam.

00:09:45.749 --> 00:09:48.030
They don't want to provide
their personal information,

00:09:48.030 --> 00:09:49.260
and they just simply do nothing.

00:09:49.260 --> 00:09:51.720
And this particular
settlement provides that

00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:52.730
if they don't do anything,

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:55.100
they will at least get a
thousand virtual dollars.

00:09:55.100 --> 00:09:56.680
Theoretically, also you could write

00:09:56.680 --> 00:09:58.510
into the settlement
administrator and you could say

00:09:58.510 --> 00:10:00.020
that you don't want to participate

00:10:00.020 --> 00:10:01.360
in this settlement agreement

00:10:01.360 --> 00:10:03.410
and you can exclude
yourself from the class.

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:05.970
The main benefit there
is that regardless of

00:10:05.970 --> 00:10:08.370
what happens in the class,
you might be able to file suit

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:10.900
on your own behalf, but
you'd never want to do that

00:10:10.900 --> 00:10:13.650
because the dollar amounts
are way, way too small.

00:10:13.650 --> 00:10:15.870
And additionally, you can
also attend the hearing

00:10:15.870 --> 00:10:17.450
on this settlement agreement.

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:19.770
Because right now we're in the
preliminary approval stage.

00:10:19.770 --> 00:10:21.650
The court has looked at this settlement.

00:10:21.650 --> 00:10:23.870
Both the plaintiffs and the
defendants are advocating

00:10:23.870 --> 00:10:26.150
that the court should
approve this settlement,

00:10:26.150 --> 00:10:27.490
but they need more information.

00:10:27.490 --> 00:10:28.990
They need to know how
many people are going

00:10:28.990 --> 00:10:30.550
to sign up for the class.

00:10:30.550 --> 00:10:32.200
They need to know how many people object,

00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:34.550
how many people don't want
to be included in this class.

00:10:34.550 --> 00:10:35.840
Because if there are too many people

00:10:35.840 --> 00:10:38.580
who reject the settlement,
then the court might have

00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:40.870
to tell the parties to go
back to the drawing board.

00:10:40.870 --> 00:10:42.860
And here's one of the craziest things.

00:10:42.860 --> 00:10:45.930
Sometimes if too many people
sign up for the benefits

00:10:45.930 --> 00:10:47.810
of the settlement agreement,

00:10:47.810 --> 00:10:49.210
it kind of blows up the whole deal.

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:51.460
We saw this in the Equifax class action,

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:54.680
where they offered up to $150 per person

00:10:54.680 --> 00:10:56.530
whose privacy rights were violated

00:10:56.530 --> 00:10:58.520
when Equifax completely screwed the pooch

00:10:58.520 --> 00:11:00.170
in terms of user privacy.

00:11:00.170 --> 00:11:04.110
And then so many people
signed up to get the $150,

00:11:04.110 --> 00:11:06.150
it broke the bank and the parties had

00:11:06.150 --> 00:11:07.960
to go back to the drawing board again.

00:11:07.960 --> 00:11:10.776
And theoretically, since
I'm publicizing this video,

00:11:10.776 --> 00:11:12.935
that might happen here, too.

00:11:12.935 --> 00:11:15.130
Yeah, sorry about that.

00:11:15.130 --> 00:11:16.500
But effectively this is the same process

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:18.850
that everyone goes through
in class action settlements.

00:11:18.850 --> 00:11:21.330
It starts with notifying
the potential class,

00:11:21.330 --> 00:11:23.110
usually through email, but maybe it's

00:11:23.110 --> 00:11:26.190
through the telephone,
using these jenky notices

00:11:26.190 --> 00:11:27.630
that look like a scam.

00:11:27.630 --> 00:11:29.180
Then you have to go to these websites

00:11:29.180 --> 00:11:33.130
that look like they came
out of Geocities in 1994.

00:11:33.130 --> 00:11:35.850
And you then have to provide
your personal information

00:11:35.850 --> 00:11:37.434
to sign up for the class on the hopes

00:11:37.434 --> 00:11:39.380
that you'll get some sort of payout

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:41.080
from the settlement agreement.

00:11:41.080 --> 00:11:42.350
And of course, then you have to wait

00:11:42.350 --> 00:11:44.660
for the court to approve
the final settlement.

00:11:44.660 --> 00:11:47.110
And then maybe a year or two later,

00:11:47.110 --> 00:11:49.990
you might actually get a check in the mail

00:11:49.990 --> 00:11:54.310
or some virtual dollars
deposited into your bank account.

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:56.370
It takes a very, very long time.

